 <!-- About Section -->
 <section class="about-section">
     <div class="auto-container">
         <div class="row">
             <div class="col-lg-6">
                 <div class="about-content-block">
                     <h1>Mediation: A Voluntary and Neutral Path to Amicable Resolution</h1>
                     <div class="text wow fadeInUp" style="color:black;text-align:justify;" data-wow-delay="200ms">Mediation is a voluntary process where a neutral and independent mediator helps people in a dispute talk to each other and find a solution that works for everyone. It gives both sides a chance to openly share their concerns and feelings, and then jointly explore solutions that suit their needs. The mediator does not make decisions or force any outcome, but supports the discussion in a positive and respectful environment so the parties can reach a friendly and mutual agreement.</div>
                     <div class="row">
                           <div class="col-lg-12">
      <div class="about-content-block">
                          <div class="text wow fadeInUp" style="color:black;text-align:justify;" data-wow-delay="200ms">
                      <h3 class="benefits-heading">Benefits of Mediation?</h3>

<ul class="benefits-mediation">
    <li>Mediation is faster and generally less expensive than a trial.</li>
    <li>There is more flexibility, allowing creative and practical solutions.</li>
    <li>Allows parties to express their views informally and confidentially.</li>
    <li>Parties work out solutions that meet their interests.</li>
    <li>Focuses on the future rather than past disputes.</li>
    <li>Eliminates the risks of litigation.</li>
    <li>Helps save time, energy, money, and relationships.</li>
    <li>Creates harmony through a win-win outcome.</li>
</ul>
             </div></div></div>
                     </div>
                     
                 </div>
             </div>
             <div class="col-lg-6">
